  "caveats": [
    "The stepped empty corner is the layout of the camera's four detectors, not a feature of the nebula.",
    "Around the bright star in the lower left, the straight vertical streak and the small ring above it are camera effects (charge spilling along a detector column and a reflection inside the camera), not gas. A thin straight line in the sky right of the left pillar is also a camera blemish.",
    "Star spikes come from the telescope's support struts; they point in slightly different directions in the two images because the telescope was turned differently.",
    "Colors are assigned, not seen by eye."
  ],
